cellSpurs: _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody (NID 0x8A85674D) and the guest queue layout written by _cellSpursLFQueueInitialize.

Games: A Crack in Time 1.20 imports _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody (Edge job push: func_00717068 non-blocking, func_00717358
blocking) and had no handler (the dispatcher faked CELL_OK, so pushed jobs never reached the SPU consumer). Tools of Destruction
uses the same import (submit 0x616da8, wait 0x6173c8) and the same Initialize.
Spec and evidence: work/reports/lfqueue-layout-acit.md (main checkout; SPU consumer lifts ACiT elf_00be3800, ToD elf_008ea200).
RPCS3 cellSync is a behaviour reference only (GPL-2, nothing copied).

Initialize: +0x00..+0x0F stay zero (the old code wrote the depth at +0x0C, which is the h7 "waiting" flag and, for direction 3, a
waiting-producer pack); depth at +0x14, size +0x10, buffer EA +0x18, direction +0x24, init flag +0x2C, eaSignal +0x70, rest zero.
Push (isBlocking, queue 128-aligned, element 16-aligned): NULL -> 0x80410111, misaligned -> 0x80410110, direction not 2/3 ->
0x80410109, full and non-blocking -> 0x80410901, full and blocking -> wait (1 ms sleeps; optional g_rc_lfq_stop_requested hook, never
drops the element), else 0. Per element: reserve (h8 at +0x0E, full if (h8-h1) mod 2*depth >= depth), copy the element to
buffer + size*(slot >= depth ? slot-depth : slot), publish h5 (+0x08) with the out-of-order bitmap h6 (+0x0A) after the data, then
wake one waiting consumer through spu_taskset_signal_task(eaSignal & ~1, id). Reserve and publish each run under the line's
lock-line lock (the SPU's GETLLAR/PUTLLC serialise on it) with raw stores and one spu_coh_notify_write, i.e. one atomic update of
the 128-byte line; patch 1111's store path is not changed. The first 3 pushes dump the whole line before and after.
Also adds the NID name to tools/nid_database.py.

ASSUMPTIONs:
 - direction numbering SPU2SPU 0, SPU2PPU 1, PPU2SPU 2, ANY2ANY 3 (ACiT passes 3, ToD 2);
 - 0x80410901 (TASK-series AGAIN) is what a full non-blocking push returns (only evidence: the game tests exactly that);
 - isBlocking != 0 waits for a slot (no lv2 event queue: Attach is log-only);
 - waiting-consumer ring: pack u16 at +0x30 (direction 2) or +0x04 (direction 3, inferred from the SPU shuffle, no producer code
   exists), ids u16 x15 at +0x32; tail = bits 0-4, head = bits 10-14, indices 0..29, wrap 29 -> 0, id slot = idx mod 15;
 - a producer never sets the waiting-producer flag (+0x0C bit 1 / pack at +0x0C or +0x50): it polls instead;
 - the buffer EA low bit is set for direction 3 (the ACiT consumer masks it) and masked on push;
 - init flag value 1 at +0x2C; +0x20 bs[4] and +0x28 stay zero;
 - bitmap h6: bit k = slot h5+1+k completed ahead of h5 (the SPU consumer never reads it);
 - the signal target `eaSignal & ~1` is a taskset and the waiter id is a taskset task id.

